{"toolCallId":"call_0fb5cf4c82714e488d73b023236f7951","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Fill each checklist section below. -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three rows and add the rule this packet uses for a blocked task. GOOD: P0 blocks close. P1 needs a recorded reason. WEAK: Follow the priorities. -->\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per setup fact, each with a command. GOOD: CHK-001 [P0] The start commit is in `goal.md` section 4. WEAK: Setup is ready. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file rule. A command must answer it. GOOD: CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0. WEAK: Code is clean. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Code passes lint/format checks\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No console errors or warnings\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling implemented\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows project patterns\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per acceptance criterion. GOOD: CHK-020 [P0] `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: Tests pass. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per finding class this packet can produce. Delete the rows that do not apply. GOOD: CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Every finding names one class. WEAK: All findings handled. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per security surface. Write `N/A` with a reason when none applies. GOOD: CHK-030 [P0] The script reads no credential. WEAK: Security is fine. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per document that must agree. GOOD: CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag. WEAK: Docs are updated. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file location rule. GOOD: CHK-050 [P1] Test copies live under `scratch/test/`. WEAK: Files are organized. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n<!-- FILL: Count the boxes by priority and write the three totals. GOOD: P0 12, P1 13, P2 1. WEAK: Most items done. -->\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | [X] | [ ]/[X] |\n| P1 Items | [Y] | [ ]/[Y] |\n| P2 Items | [Z] | [ ]/[Z] |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per ADR, or delete the section when the packet records no ADR. GOOD: CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T002. WEAK: Architecture is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per performance claim, or delete the section when the packet makes none. GOOD: CHK-110 [P1] The flag adds under 5 ms. WEAK: Performance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per deployment step, or delete the section when the packet ships no service. GOOD: CHK-120 [P0] The rollback command was run in a copy. WEAK: Ready to deploy. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per compliance surface, or delete the section when none applies. GOOD: CHK-130 [P1] No license changed. WEAK: Compliance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nTwo paths appear below: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` and `T` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n\nChecked before T001; these boxes are gates on the run, not tasks in the count.\n\n- [ ] The task list below is the only work order; `spec.md` §3 is the scope.\n- [ ] The baseline capture from T002 exists before the first edit to `S`.\n- [ ] No file outside the `Files to Change` row in `spec.md` is modified.\n- [ ] `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0 before the first edit.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Applies To | Requirement |\n|------|-----------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ-01 | T004, T005, T006 | The global, the parser branch and the render branch land in that order; each `Verify:` runs before the next task starts. |\n| TASK-SCOPE-01 | All tasks | Only `S` is edited. A file outside the scope stops the task and returns to the operator. |\n| TASK-VERIFY-01 | T006 onward | No task is marked `[x]` without its `Verify:` command having run and its output read. |\n| TASK-BASE-01 | T002, T010 | The default-output diff runs against the pre-change capture, never against a re-run of the changed script. |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\nReport each task as `T### <status> - <one-line evidence>`, where status is `done`, `in-progress` or `blocked`. Evidence is the observed command output, not a summary of intent.\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n\nMark the task `[B]`, record the blocking condition and the command that exposed it beneath the task, and stop the phase. A blocked task is never marked `[x]` and never silently dropped; the packet closes with the block recorded.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument `case` block and the two output functions in `S`. Verify: `rg -n -- \"'--json|-j\\)\" \"$S\"` prints the flag branch at line 706 and `rg -n 'output_text\\(\\)' \"$S\"` prints the function and its call.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the pre-change default output for the five matrix inputs into `scratch/golden/`. Verify: `ls scratch/golden/*.out \\| wc -l` prints `5`.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Inventory the consumers of `S` before touching it. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level\\.sh' .skilled --glob '!**/*.snap' --glob '!**/fixtures/**' --glob '!**/changelog/**' \\| wc -l` prints `4` call sites plus prose mentions, matching the table in `plan.md`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT` in the globals block of `S`. Verify: `rg -n '^QUIET_OUTPUT=false' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--quiet)` branch to the argument `case` in `S`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet; echo $?` prints `0` and no `Unknown option` line.\n- [ ] T006 Add the early return to `output_text()` in `S`, printing the same label line the full report prints. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet \\| wc -l` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T007 [P] Document the flag in the header OPTIONS block and in `show_help()` (OPTIONS plus one EXAMPLES entry) in `S`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help \\| grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints `2`.\n- [ ] T008 [P] Confirm `--json` precedence needs no code: the dispatch already prefers `output_json`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet --json \\| node -e 'let s=\"\";process.stdin.on(\"data\",d=>s+=d).on(\"end\",()=>{JSON.parse(s);console.log(\"ok\")})'` prints `ok`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Run the quiet form for all five matrix inputs. Verify: each run prints `1` line and the label text matches `plan.md` §5.\n- [ ] T010 Diff the default run against the T002 capture for all five inputs. Verify: `diff scratch/golden/<name>.out <(bash \"$S\" <args>)` prints nothing for every fixture.\n- [ ] T011 Run the two Node fixtures that parse `--json`. Verify: `node \"$T/test-phase-system.js\"` and `node \"$T/test-phase-validation.js\"` each print `failed=0`.\n- [ ] T012 Check syntax and the error paths. Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0, `bash \"$S\" --loc abc --quiet` exits 1 with empty stdout, and `bash \"$S\" --quie` still exits 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] The five-input byte diff is empty and both Node fixtures report `failed=0`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md` (ADR-001 to ADR-003 in the L3 Architecture Decision Record)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA blocked P0 stays open. A P1 may close with a recorded reason in the task that owns it. A P2 may defer with one sentence saying why.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Verify: `rg -c 'REQ-00[1-6]' spec.md` prints `6`.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md. Verify: `rg -c 'ADR-00[1-3]' plan.md` prints at least `6`.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available. Verify: `bash --version` and `command -v wc sed diff grep node` each resolve.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0 after the edit.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No stderr output on a valid quiet run. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null \\| wc -l` prints `0`.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] The parser still rejects a value-taking flag with no value. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc --quiet` exits 1 with `--loc requires a numeric value`.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The new branch matches the surrounding style: same `case` shape, same `shift`, no new helper.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria in `acceptance-criteria.md` are met, each with observed evidence.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete: the five matrix inputs run in both forms.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested: no arguments, non-numeric value, unknown option, maximum inputs.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated: stdout empty and exit 1 on every invalid input, with `--quiet` present.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets. Verify: `rg -n 'SECRET\\|TOKEN\\|PASSWORD\\|API_KEY' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged: `LOC`, `FILES` and `PHASE_THRESHOLD` still pass the same `^[0-9]+$` checks.\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] No auth or authorization surface exists: the flag reads no credential and opens no network path.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized. Verify: `rg -c -- '--quiet' spec.md plan.md tasks.md` reports a non-zero count for each.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate: the header OPTIONS block and `show_help()` both name the flag and its `--json` interaction.\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable): `runtime/cli/spec/README.md` describes the script without listing flags, so it needs no edit.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in `scratch/` only. Verify: `git status --porcelain` lists no new file outside `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/`.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` cleaned before completion. Verify: `ls scratch/golden` is empty or removed.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 11 | [ ]/11 |\n| P1 Items | 20 | [ ]/20 |\n| P2 Items | 9 | [ ]/9 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 to ADR-003 in `plan.md` are each followed by the task that implements them (T004 to T007).\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] Every ADR carries a status of Proposed or Accepted.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Every ADR names at least one rejected alternative with its reason.\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented: not applicable, the flag is additive and the default path is unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 holds: `time bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet` stays within the default run's wall clock.\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput target is not set; the script serves one caller per invocation.\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing not applicable: single-shot CLI with no shared state.\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Record the wall clock of one quiet and one default run in `scratch/` during T009.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented in `plan.md` §7 and exercised on a copy of the script.\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] No rollout flag is needed: the default output is unchanged, so the change ships inert for existing callers.\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] No monitoring surface exists; the script emits no telemetry.\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook is the single revert in `plan.md` §7 plus the two verification commands.\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Rollback runbook reviewed against a copy of the script before close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review: the flag adds no input class, no file path and no network call.\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses unchanged; no dependency is added.\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP checklist not applicable: local CLI with no network, auth or data handling.\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling: the script reads numeric arguments and prints scores; it stores nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `acceptance-criteria.md` agree on the flag name and the one-line contract.\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] The CLI's API is its `--help` text, and that text names the flag in both blocks.\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing docs: the follow-up in `plan.md` affected surfaces covers the playbook transcript.\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer: the header comment records the flag and the `--json` precedence rule.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":92,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":103}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
