] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: producer/helper/policy] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: what owns the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: consumer/status/docs/tests] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: how it observes the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Components/functions] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: API endpoints/flows] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Tools] |\n| Manual | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/Library] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Internal/External] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Green/Yellow/Red] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n- **Trigger**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Draw the phase order in the fence, then fill the table with depends-on and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup to Implementation to Verification. Verification blocks close. WEAK: Phases depend on each other. -->\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n<!-- FILL: Give each phase an estimate and a total. Mark the total as an assumption. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup 10 minutes, implementation 30, verification 10. Total 50 minutes. WEAK: A few hours. -->\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger, the steps and the data reversal. Write `No` when no data changes. Delete the whole section when the packet ships no deployable service. GOOD: Trigger: default output changes. Steps: revert one commit, rerun the two commands. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n<!-- FILL: Draw the component order and fill the matrix with produces and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Script to test to close. WEAK: Components depend on each other. -->\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component A] | None | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | B, C |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component B] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component C] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component D] | B, C | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n<!-- FILL: Name the longest chain and its total. List what can run in parallel. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Implementation to verification, 40 minutes. Docs run in parallel. WEAK: The critical path is the main path. -->\n\n1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task A] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task C] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n<!-- FILL: Name three milestones with a command-checkable success criterion. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: M1: the branch exists. `rg -n quiet` prints it. WEAK: Milestones are tracked. -->\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Setup Complete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All dependencies ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Core Done] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Main features working] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Release Ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All tests pass] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n<!-- FILL: Write one ADR per decision. Name the context, the choice, the consequence and the rejected option. GOOD: ADR-001: a flag, because callers already pass flags. WEAK: We made a decision. -->\n\n### ADR-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Positive outcome 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Option B]: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one boolean flag and one early-return branch to a single bash script. The branch renders the label line the full report already prints, and a five-input byte diff proves the default path did not move.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2+ (macOS system bash) |\n| **Framework** | None - one standalone shell script |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | `bash -n`, `wc -l`, `diff`, and the existing Node fixtures under `runtime/cli/tests/` |\n\n### Overview\n\nChange one bash script: add a `QUIET_OUTPUT` global, one `--quiet` branch in the existing argument `case`, and one early-return inside `output_text()`. The early return prints the same label line the full report prints, so the format stays defined in one place. Prove it with a line count of 1 on the quiet run and an empty diff against a pre-change capture of the default run for five inputs.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n- [ ] Baseline default output captured for all five matrix inputs\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `bash -n` exits 0 and both Node fixtures report `failed=0`\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks) and the help surfaces name the flag\n- [ ] The default-output diff is empty for all five inputs\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\n\nSingle script, one render branch.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`recommend-level.sh` §5): the `case` block that turns argv into globals. `--quiet` joins it as a boolean with no argument.\n- **`output_text()`** (§4): the only place the human report is rendered. The quiet branch is an early return here, so the label literal stays beside the full report.\n- **`show_help()` and the header comment**: the two documentation surfaces inside the file. Both list every flag, so both must list `--quiet`.\n\n### Data Flow\n\nargv → parser sets `LOC`, `FILES`, the risk flags, `JSON_OUTPUT` and `QUIET_OUTPUT` → numeric validation → `calculate_*_score` → `determine_level` → `calculate_confidence` → output dispatch. `output_json` runs when `JSON_OUTPUT` is true; otherwise `output_text` runs, and its first statement returns the one-line form when `QUIET_OUTPUT` is true. Scoring never reads `QUIET_OUTPUT`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\nThe change is additive, but it edits a script with live callers, so the consumer inventory is the part that prevents a regression.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Producer: owns parsing, scoring and rendering | update | `bash -n` exits 0; `--quiet \\| wc -l` prints 1 |\n| `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan.yaml` | Consumer: P1 pre-workflow step calls it with `--json` | unchanged | `rg -n 'recommend-level'` still shows the `--json` call and no `--quiet` |\n| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` | Consumer: parses `--json` fixtures | unchanged | `node .../test-phase-system.js` prints `failed=0` |\n| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js` | Consumer: parses `--json` fixtures | unchanged | `node .../test-phase-validation.js` prints `failed=0` |\n| `manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md` | Consumer: runs `--help` and transcribes the OPTIONS block | update (follow-up, outside this packet's write scope) | after the follow-up, `rg -n -- '--quiet'` finds the new line |\n| `runtime/cli/spec/README.md` | Prose: one-line description of the script | unchanged | `rg -n 'recommend-level'` shows a description with no flag list |\n| Prose references under `references/`, `feature-catalog/`, `assets/`, `SKILL.md` | Documentation, never executed | not a consumer | The consumer inventory command below lists them |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n -- \"'--json|-j\\)|'--help|-h\\)|--recommend-phases\\)|--no-recommend-phases\\)\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`. Every flag branch lives in one `case` block, so the new branch joins a single producer.\n- Consumers of the changed surface: `rg -n 'recommend-level\\.sh' .skilled --glob '!**/*.snap' --glob '!**/fixtures/**' --glob '!**/changelog/**'`. Four call sites, listed above.\n- Matrix axes: quiet (on/off) x json (on/off) x help (on/off) x input (valid/invalid) x phase output (on/off). The rows this packet must run are in §5.\n- Algorithm invariant: `TOTAL_SCORE`, `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `CONFIDENCE` are computed before any output call and must not read `QUIET_OUTPUT`. For any input, the quiet line equals line 2 of the default run.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nThe matrix below is the pre-change baseline, measured against the current script on 2026-10-25. The implementation must reproduce the `Default lines` column exactly and must return the same label text on the quiet run.\n\n| Input | Default lines | Label line |\n|-------|---------------|------------|\n| `--loc 200 --files 5 --api` | 16 | `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)` |\n| `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` | 17 | `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)` |\n| `--loc 50 --files 2` | 16 | `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)` |\n| `--loc 100 --files 3 --no-recommend-phases` | 12 | `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)` |\n| `--loc 12 --files 1` | 16 | `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)` |\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | `output_text()` quiet branch and the parser branch | `bash -n`, `wc -l`, `sed -n '2p'`, `diff` |\n| Integration | The `--json` path still parses after the change | `node .../tests/test-phase-system.js`, `node .../tests/test-phase-validation.js` |\n| Manual | `--help` reads correctly and names the flag once per block | Terminal |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| `bash` 3.2+ with `[[ ]]` and `case` | Internal | Green | Already required by the script; no new construct is introduced |\n| `wc`, `sed`, `diff`, `grep` | Internal | Green | Verification only; absence blocks proof, not the change |\n| `node` for the existing fixtures | Internal | Green | If unavailable, the JSON regression proof falls back to a manual parse with `node -e` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: The default (non-quiet) output changes by one byte for any matrix input, or `--json` output changes shape.\n- **Procedure**: `git revert <commit>` for the single commit, then rerun the five-input diff and both Node fixtures to confirm the pre-change bytes are back.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Baseline) ─┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core |\n| Baseline capture | Setup | Core, Verify |\n| Core | Setup, Baseline capture | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 20 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 15 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **~45 minutes (assumption; one file, ~12 lines)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes) - no data changes\n- [ ] Feature flag configured - the flag itself is the only switch\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set - none exist for this script\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the single commit with `git revert`.\n2. Rerun the five-input diff against the pre-change capture.\n3. Confirm both Node fixtures report `failed=0`.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: Not applicable - the script writes no file and holds no state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Help text │\n                    │  (parallel)│\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture (T002) | None | Five golden output files | Core, Verify |\n| Parser branch (T005) | `QUIET_OUTPUT` global (T004) | A recognized flag | Render branch |\n| Render branch (T006) | Parser branch | One-line stdout | Verification |\n| Help text (T007) | Parser branch | `--help` entry and header comment | Docs check |\n| Verification (T009-T012) | Render branch, help text | Line counts, diffs, fixture results | Close |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **T004-T006: global, parser branch, render branch** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **T009-T010: line counts and byte diff** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **T012: syntax and fixture run** - 5 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: ~35 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- T007 (help text) and T008 (`--json` precedence check) run beside T006 once the parser branch exists.\n- T003 (consumer inventory) runs during Setup and does not block T004.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Flag parses | `recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet; echo $?` prints `0` | End of Phase 2 start |\n| M2 | One line | `recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet \\| wc -l` prints `1` | End of Phase 2 |\n| M3 | No regression | Five-input diff is empty and both Node fixtures report `failed=0` | End of Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Render the quiet line inside `output_text()`\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: The quiet output is one line that already exists inside the full report. A separate render function would have to repeat the label literal, and the two copies could drift when the label changes.\n\n**Decision**: Make the quiet branch the first statement of `output_text()`, returning after it prints the same interpolation the full report uses.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- The label format is defined once, next to the report that also prints it.\n- `output_text()` gains a second exit path; the early return must stay above every other `echo` or a stray blank line breaks the one-line contract.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- A separate `output_quiet()` function: duplicates the label literal, which is exactly the drift the change should avoid.\n- Branching in the main dispatch (`if quiet; then ... else output_text; fi`): moves the label away from the report and gives the script a second output entry point.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: `--json` takes precedence over `--quiet`\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: `--json` is a machine contract with three live callers that parse it. `--quiet` asks for a one-line text form. Combining them has no single obvious meaning.\n\n**Decision**: `--quiet` affects `output_text()` only. When `JSON_OUTPUT` is true, `output_json` runs and `--quiet` has no effect.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- No existing JSON caller can receive text, even if it later adds `--quiet` for another reason.\n- A caller that wants one JSON field must still parse the document; `--quiet` does not become a second JSON mode.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Reject the combination with an error: fails a harmless call for no benefit.\n- Quiet over JSON: prints text into a stream every JSON caller parses, which is the one outcome that breaks them.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-003: Long flag only, no `-q`\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: The script already carries short aliases for `--json` (`-j`) and `--help` (`-h`), so symmetry would suggest `-q`.\n\n**Decision**: Add `--quiet` only.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- One spelling to document and to keep in sync with `--help`.\n- A caller that wants a short form must wait for a request that justifies it.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Add `-q` for symmetry: a second spelling with no caller, and one more line in every help surface.\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":122,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":79}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
